    {
      "id": "SCM-01",
      "chapter": "inputs",
      "title": "Standard split pairs identify the columns with ordinary unimodular lists",
      "anchor": "inputs-split-columns",
      "statement": "If a+s≤n, every ordered split list of length a is carried by GL_n(R) to any prescribed distinct coordinate pairs. With this list fixed, every vertical b-cycle bounds when b+s≤n−a.",
      "hypotheses": "R a commutative ring with identity, stable range at most s, a,b,n,s natural. A plain unimodular list must admit simultaneous duals. The split list includes the chosen duals.",
      "definitions": [
        "At every d≥s a unimodular row of length d+1 shortens to length d by adding multiples of its last entry.",
        "The boundaries delete from the split list or the plain list separately. Their squares vanish and hv=vh.",
        "If s=0, the unit-ideal condition on the empty row forces 0=1."
      ],
